    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I reproduced this on latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nAdding a treesitter language in `40_plugins.lua` cause an error message when opening a file of the added language.\n\nExpected behavior: No error message, should just open cleanly.\nOS: Debian 13\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Perform clean install with `setup.lua`\n2. On line `58` of `40_plugins.lua` add any treesitter supported language to `languages` (e.g. `python`)\n3. Save `40_plugins.lua` and exit Neovim.\n4. Open a file of the corresponding language type directly using the `nvim` command (e.g. `nvim file.py`)\n5. See error message similar to:\n```\nError in BufNewFile Autocommands for \"*\":                                                                                                                                                                            \nLua callback: /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:28: BufNewFile Autocommands for \"*\"..FileType Autocommands for \"python\": Vim(append):Lua callback: /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/treesitter.lua:460:\n Parser could not be created for buffer 1 and language \"python\"                                                                                                                                                      \nstack traceback:                                                                                                                                                                                                     \n        [C]: in function 'assert'                                                                                                                                                                                    \n        /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/treesitter.lua:460: in function 'start'                                                                                                                                \n        /home/user1/.config/nvim/plugin/40_plugins.lua:79: in function </home/user1/.config/nvim/plugin/40_plugins.lua:79>                                                                             \n        [C]: in function 'nvim_cmd'                                                                                                                                                                                  \n        /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:28: in function </usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:27>                                                                                                   \n        [C]: in function 'pcall'                                                                                                                                                                                     \n        vim/_core/shared.lua: in function <vim/_core/shared.lua:0>                                                                                                                                                   \n        [C]: in function '_with'                                                                                                                                                                                     \n        /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:27: in function </usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:10>                                                                                                   \nstack traceback:                                                                                                                                                                                                     \n        [C]: in function '_with'                                                                                                                                                                                     \n        /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:27: in function </usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/filetype.lua:10>\n```",
