        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!  \n\n> 2. On line `58` of `40_plugins.lua` add any treesitter supported language to `languages` (e.g. `python`)\n> \n> 3. Open a file of the corresponding language type directly using the `nvim` command (e.g. `nvim file.py`)\n\nSome steps are missing here. I presume, `nvim file.py` is run immediately after adding the 'python' language and closing Neovim, right? If yes, then this is expected since tree-sitter parser installation is not immediate (i.e. asynchronous) while opening `nvim file.py` needs 'python' parser to exists immediately after startup is finished.\n\nAfter changing which languages are used, there needs to be a restart which *will not* require using new parser(s) at startup. After installation, it can be opened freely, though.\n\nI'll adjust the documentation to mention this.",
